WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:07.470
My name is Anni Beukes. I'm a fellow the
Mansueto Institute for urban

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:11.460
Innovation at the University of Chicago.
I've just joined the Institute after

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:15.420
spending almost five years that Slum Dwellers International at Secretariat

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:20.400
in Cape Town my research in my work both
in research and practice is really

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:25.770
around the connection or the
intersection between poverty, politics, and

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:31.710
place and I try to work with
communities and support their visions around

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:36.060
how they think and imagine there are
settlements to be. At the core in the

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:40.610
talk that I gave today was to to share
with students some of the challenges of

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:45.270
urbanization in sub-saharan Africa
what these challenges would mean both in

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:49.260
terms of physical infrastructure but
also rapid social change that we are

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:53.520
seeing I'm very excited about the youth
of Africa because that's we have the

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:57.809
biggest youth population in sub-saharan
Africa and that for me really is the

00:00:57.809 --> 00:01:00.660
core of what is going to drive
sustainable and equitable development

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:05.309
when we pay attention to what it is that
young people imagine, what they aspire to,

00:01:05.309 --> 00:01:10.110
and create the kinds of environments
that will give them a space from which

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:14.490
to launch their biggest dreams for our
planet and for their own well-being

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:17.479
and prosperity.

